591 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Systems engineer: Systems engineers are responsible for scoping, developing, and supporting core gameplay systems. They often work in the low-level side of the engine to create systems for game features, developer tooling, and optimization. This work may touch a variety of different systems including streaming, SDKs, threading, memory management, and platform and middleware abstractions. Junior programmers interested in this role should participate in engine development projects and study system architecture.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
592 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
