944 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The STAR method, which stands for Situation, Task, Action, and Result, is a common approach where interviewers often frame questions to be best addressed using this structured format.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
945 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Watch for questions that prompt you to describe past situations, discuss specific challenges, or detail achieved results. When responding, structure your answers to articulate the situation or task, the actions you took, and the positive outcomes attained. This method provides a systematic way to highlight your problem-solving and decision-making skills, aligning seamlessly with the industry's interview expectations. Utilizing the STAR method enables you to stay focused, respond succinctly, and demonstrate your skills with the interviewer's preferred format, leaving a lasting positive impression.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
